{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.DFrameClosedFormExponents","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrameClosedFormExponents","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.IntervalCases","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.deuteron_uExp_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.deuteron_uExp_gap","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameClosedFormExponents.lean#L153-L154","doc":"…and the gap is exactly the `−6` the bean recorded (C minus D). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.deuteron_uExp_differs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.deuteron_uExp_differs","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameClosedFormExponents.lean#L149-L151","doc":"The deuteron is *not* on the agreement line — the frames genuinely differ\nthere, by the `+6` recorded in `qou-iayk`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.helium3_unique_uExp_agreement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.helium3_unique_uExp_agreement","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameClosedFormExponents.lean#L134-L147","doc":"**³He is the unique light atom where the two `u`-exponents agree.**\n\n`qou-iayk` recorded that ³He matched the convention-C exponent exactly\n(58 = 58) while its mass-3 partner tritium was off by 5, and read the\nirregularity as evidence the fresh values were incoherent. They are not:\n`(Z,N) = (2,1)` is simply the one point with `N ≤ 2` lying on the agreement\nline `6Z + N = 13`.\n\nThe bound on `Z` is not needed: `N ≤ 2` alone forces `6Z ∈ {11,12,13}`, hence\n`Z = 2`. Stated without it, since carrying a hypothesis the proof does not use\nwould overstate what the result requires. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.uExp_agree_iff_A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.uExp_agree_iff_A","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameClosedFormExponents.lean#L129-L132","doc":"The same line in the `(A, Z)` coordinates the law is usually written in. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.uExp_agree_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.uExp_agree_iff","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameClosedFormExponents.lean#L118-L127","doc":"The two `u`-exponents agree **iff `6Z + N = 13`** (equivalently\n`A + 5Z = 13`).\n\nThis is a codimension-1 line in `(Z,N)`, not a coincidence — see\n`helium3_unique_uExp_agreement` for why one atom appeared to satisfy the\nC-frame law exactly while its mass-3 partner did not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.cycloExp_agree_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.cycloExp_agree_iff","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameClosedFormExponents.lean#L106-L116","doc":"**Convention C is blind to the proton/neutron distinction, and this says\nexactly how.**\n\nThe two cyclotomic exponents agree **iff `N = 0`** — i.e. only on\npure-proton configurations. Under C every nucleon contributes 3; under D a\nproton contributes 3 and a neutron 1, so the frames coincide precisely when\nthere are no neutrons. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.uExpD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.uExpD","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameClosedFormExponents.lean#L103-L104","doc":"`u`-exponent measured in convention D: `12Z + 20N + 14`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.uExpC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.uExpC","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameClosedFormExponents.lean#L100-L101","doc":"`u`-exponent of the landed convention-C law: `18Z + 21N + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.cycloExpD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.cycloExpD","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameClosedFormExponents.lean#L97-L98","doc":"Cyclotomic exponent measured in convention D: `A + 2Z − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.cycloExpC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.cycloExpC","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameClosedFormExponents.lean#L94-L95","doc":"Cyclotomic exponent of the landed convention-C law: `3A − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zD_at_usq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zD_at_usq","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameClosedFormExponents.lean#L84-L90","doc":"Convention D at `q = u²`: `z_D = u⁶/(1+u⁴)`.\n\nThe cleared factor is `(1+u⁴)`, **not** `(1+u²)` — so the landed law's\ncyclotomic base cannot survive the convention change. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.clearedDenom_C_ne_D","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.clearedDenom_C_ne_D","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameClosedFormExponents.lean#L61-L82","doc":"**The two frames clear genuinely different denominators.**\n\nAt `q = u²` convention C's `z` is `u/(1+u²)` and convention D's is\n`u⁶/(1+u⁴)`. The landed law's cyclotomic factor is the *first* denominator\ncleared once per Markov peel, so the only way it survives the convention\nchange is if the two denominators coincide — and they do not, for any `u`\noutside `{0, ±1}`.\n\nAn earlier draft of this file stated the C form as `u/(u²+1) = u/(u²+1)`,\nwhich is `rfl` and says nothing. This is the non-vacuous statement it was\nreaching for. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zC_spelling_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zC_spelling_eq","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameClosedFormExponents.lean#L46-L59","doc":"**The detector-blind convention-C spelling.**\n\n`1/(s + s⁻¹) = s/(q+1)` whenever `s² = q`. Writing `s` for `√q`, the\nleft-hand side is `d_u_closed_form_proof.py:18`'s\n`z = 1/(q^(1/2) + q^(-1/2))` and the right-hand side is `√q/(q+1)` = `z_C`.\n\nThis is the identity that makes a grep for the convention-C *form* miss the\nlanded proof, and it is the load-bearing step of the `qou-iayk`\nadjudication. ","signatureChunk":0}]}